        {
          "id": "overview_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h3",
          "text": "Overview: Temperature Layering Strategy"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview_body",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "body",
          "text": "October offers ideal trekking conditions with daytime temperatures around 10-15°C and nighttime lows near -10°C. Success depends on a layering system that manages moisture while providing insulation. This packing list accounts for the dramatic temperature swings between hiking hours and stationary periods at teahouses."
        },
        {
          "id": "context_section",
          "component": "Column",
          "children": [
            "context_title",
            "context_body"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "context_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h3",
          "text": "Context and Assumptions"
        },
        {
          "id": "context_body",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "body",
          "text": "This list assumes a 10-day teahouse-based trek with porter support (duffel bag carried separately from your daypack). The temperature range -10°C to 15°C reflects typical October conditions at varying elevations. All clothing recommendations prioritize merino wool and synthetic materials over cotton. Estimated total weight for duffel bag: 10-12 kg; daypack: 5-7 kg."
        },
